"severe strain\"*** — and it comes **weeks after Washington lifted sanctions on Ethiopia and Eritrea tied to atrocities from that last war, saying the *\"national emergency… has expired.\"*** And **Ethiopia's president, addressing the UN General Assembly, placed the blame for the collapse of the agreement inside the federal government itself**, saying *\"This war has been in the making for a while now. Much of the provisions in the cessation of hostilities were primarily sabotaged by the federal government itself,\"* citing **fuel, service and cash restrictions imposed on Tigray and the government's failure to set up the interim administration the deal had promised** — *\"What was supposed to be an interim arrangement turned out to be permanent,\"* with Tigray excluded from national elections since. **The cause is a war entering its second week of open fighting in which the command's stated posture is restraint, the accusation has moved to Eritrea by name and been denied, the blackout and the drones are both now reported against civilians, and the head of state is describing the collapse of the last peace from the platform of the UN.**",
