   "**But the hearing on Thursday is a lever, and the three reforms identified on Friday are still technical and available** — the moment agent access to systems it has no authorisation to use is denied by default rather than policed by intent, the moment a short statutory window obliges developers to report anomalous agent behaviour to a named authority instead of an unread public mailbox, and the moment states publish standing terms for machine access so authorised retrieval is distinguishable from intrusion, the effect changes from a breach discovered by luck in a review to one detected and declared as a matter of course. §23 states where the warning against this is lodged."
