  "verse": "If you heed yourselves inwardly, then you will be warned through your admonishment (conscience) against all inequitableness and against all unfairness (irresponsibility), as well as against all unrighteousness, so that you can then decide what you must do and what you must leave undone.",
  "verseSrc": "Chapter 19, Verse 23",
  "hinge": "The cause is not the rogue agent — an agent that keeps trying until it succeeds is doing what it was built to do. It is the choice to field a capability that acts at machine speed while arranging its accountability at the speed of a stated willingness to attend: access granted by default, breach notified late to a mailbox, liability left unassigned, and the rule left to be drafted out of a conversation with the parties whose conduct it would govern. §23 locates the warning precisely — *\"through your admonishment (conscience)… you can then decide what you must do and what you have to leave undone.\"* The decision of what to leave undone is the whole of AI governance, and it belongs to the developers, the Senate and the agencies that publish the systems, not to the model. Australia now has the two named witnesses, the remit that reaches water and energy as well as safety, and a hearing date. Whether the firms appear, what they concede on the record, and whether the inquiry converts a conversation into a statutory reporting window to a named authority — default-deny machine access, a fixed disclosure clock, public standing terms — is a matter of what the legislature chooses to require rather than of what the technology permits."
